<title>UK: BT to take 500 mln stg charge in Q2.</title>
<headline>BT to take 500 mln stg charge in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc said on Thursday it would take a 500 million stg charge for its share of the government's windfall tax in the second quarter.  </p>
<p>The charge is payable in two instalments in December 1997 and 1998. Although BT feels the tax is unjustified, it says it will not challenge the levy in the courts.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7987</p>
